---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Financial & Tax Disclaimer"
  description="NetWageTax is an independent educational calculation utility. It is not a CPA or tax advisor, does not file tax returns, and is not affiliated with the IRS."
>
  <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 sm:text-4xl">Financial &amp; Tax Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Effective and last updated: {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-500/10 p-5 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200" role="note">
      <p class="font-semibold">Please read before relying on any result.</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        NetWageTax is an educational calculation utility. It is not a certified public accountant (CPA), enrolled
        agent, tax attorney, or registered tax advisor. It does not prepare or file tax returns, and it is not
        affiliated with, endorsed by, or acting on behalf of the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) or any other government
        agency.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="educational">Educational purposes only</h2>
    <p>
      All calculators, articles, explanations, and examples on NetWageTax are provided for general informational and
      educational purposes. They are designed to help you understand how U.S. tax rules generally work, such as how a
      deduction cap or an income phase-out is applied. They are not a substitute for individualized advice from a
      qualified professional who knows your complete financial situation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-professional">Not a professional advisor</h2>
    <p>
      NetWageTax and its operators are not acting as your CPA, enrolled agent, attorney, financial planner, or
      fiduciary. Using the Site does not create a professional-client, advisory, or fiduciary relationship of any
      kind. Nothing on the Site is a recommendation to take, or not take, any particular tax position or financial
      action.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-irs">Not the IRS; no filing or representation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>NetWageTax is an independent website and is <strong>not affiliated with the IRS</strong>, the U.S. Department of the Treasury, the Social Security Administration, or any state tax agency.</li>
      <li>We <strong>do not prepare, sign, e-file, or submit</strong> tax returns, amended returns, or any other forms on your behalf.</li>
      <li>We <strong>do not represent taxpayers</strong> before the IRS or any state tax authority, and we cannot respond to notices, audits, or correspondence for you.</li>
      <li>Results are <strong>not official determinations</strong> of your tax liability, refund, or eligibility for any deduction or credit.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="estimates">Results are estimates</h2>
    <p>Calculator output is an estimate and may differ from your actual tax outcome because, among other things:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Results depend entirely on the accuracy and completeness of the figures you enter.</li>
      <li>
        Our tools model specific rules (for example, the OBBBA qualified tips and overtime deductions) and may simplify
        or omit interactions with other provisions, credits, alternative minimum tax, state and local taxes, or
        unusual circumstances.
      </li>
      <li>
        Tax law, IRS guidance, forms, and inflation adjustments change. New or recently enacted provisions may be
        subject to regulations and interpretations that had not been issued when a tool was last updated.
      </li>
      <li>
        Marginal-rate and savings estimates are approximations and do not account for every factor that determines
        your final tax.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="accuracy">No guarantee of accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep our calculators accurate and aligned with current law and IRS guidance, and we cite primary
      sources where practical. However, we make no representations or warranties about the accuracy, completeness,
      timeliness, or suitability of any content or result. See our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> for the full
      disclaimer of warranties and limitation of liability.
    </p>

    <h2 id="responsibility">Your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      You are solely responsible for your tax filings and for any decisions you make based on information from this
      Site. Before filing a return, adjusting your withholding, or making a financial decision, verify figures against
      official sources such as <a href="https://www.irs.gov" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">IRS.gov</a>{' '}
      and consult a qualified tax professional. NetWageTax is not responsible for any taxes, penalties, interest, or
      other losses arising from reliance on the Site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      NetWageTax is supported by advertising. Advertisements are provided by third parties and do not reflect our
      endorsement of any product or service, including any tax preparation or financial product. Our calculations
      are not influenced by advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2 id="report">Report an error</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe a calculation or explanation is incorrect or out of date, please let us know at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We review every report.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
